{
  "source": "course-assets/one-more-thing/one-more-thing.mp4",
  "duration": 223.9146875,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 3.12,
      "text": "Why can the same prompt produce a different answer?"
    },
    {
      "start": 3.78,
      "end": 6.76,
      "text": "What makes AI's answers more predictable or more varied?"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.52,
      "end": 9.64,
      "text": "And how much math does one answer require?"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.4,
      "end": 12.82,
      "text": "To answer that, let's look at a simple scenario."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.76,
      "end": 16.2,
      "text": "You ask the AI, what should I name my new dog?"
    },
    {
      "start": 16.96,
      "end": 19.26,
      "text": "For the very next open word, or token,"
    },
    {
      "start": 19.74,
      "end": 23.22,
      "text": "the AI calculates a probability for every word in its vocabulary."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.16,
      "end": 28.62,
      "text": "In this case, the name spot emerges as the top choice at 22%."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.62,
      "end": 33.52,
      "text": "But having the highest probability does not guarantee the AI will select that word."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.28,
      "end": 40.54,
      "text": "A 22% probability means AI would pick spot about 22 times out of 100 tries, on average,"
    },
    {
      "start": 41.12,
      "end": 42.22,
      "text": "if the odds stay the same."
    },
    {
      "start": 42.94,
      "end": 46.62,
      "text": "Because the system relies on probability rather than absolute certainty,"
    },
    {
      "start": 47.12,
      "end": 49.4,
      "text": "its outputs are inherently capable of variation."
    },
    {
      "start": 50.36,
      "end": 53.54,
      "text": "Let's trace how those exact odds actually play out in practice."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.54,
      "end": 64.5,
      "text": "Spot is 22%, Max 17, Buddy 14, Rex 9, Biscuit 6, and others combined at 32%."
    },
    {
      "start": 64.5,
      "end": 71.06,
      "text": "These odds remain static, making five random picks based on these odds yields one possible sequence."
    },
    {
      "start": 71.76,
      "end": 74.78,
      "text": "Max, Spot, Buddy, Rex, and Max again."
    },
    {
      "start": 75.6,
      "end": 78.84,
      "text": "Spot was picked only once, even with the highest probability."
    },
    {
      "start": 79.56,
      "end": 81.34,
      "text": "Another five picks could turn out differently."
    },
    {
      "start": 82.18,
      "end": 84.92,
      "text": "Ultimately, the best chance is not a guarantee."
    },
    {
      "start": 85.96,
      "end": 90.98,
      "text": "Choosing the most likely token every single time would make the AI's answers highly repetitive."
    },
    {
      "start": 91.86,
      "end": 94.88,
      "text": "Giving other likely tokens a chance adds necessary variety."
    },
    {
      "start": 95.68,
      "end": 99.04,
      "text": "And because each chosen token shapes the context for the one that follows,"
    },
    {
      "start": 99.5,
      "end": 103.62,
      "text": "a single different choice early on alters the entire subsequent response."
    },
    {
      "start": 105.26,
      "end": 109.18,
      "text": "Temperature reshapes the probabilities before AI picks each token."
    },
    {
      "start": 109.82,
      "end": 114.02,
      "text": "In chat GPT, Claude, and Gemini, it's handled for you behind the scenes."
    },
    {
      "start": 114.68,
      "end": 117.66,
      "text": "Low temperature concentrates probabilities toward top choices,"
    },
    {
      "start": 118.04,
      "end": 121.94,
      "text": "raising spot to 36%, while lower probability options drop."
    },
    {
      "start": 122.66,
      "end": 125.16,
      "text": "Conversely, high temperature spreads the odds out,"
    },
    {
      "start": 125.44,
      "end": 127.32,
      "text": "making less likely choices more possible."
    },
    {
      "start": 128.02,
      "end": 129.6,
      "text": "Spot falls to 16%."
    },
    {
      "start": 129.6,
      "end": 132.46,
      "text": "Ultimately, temperature reshapes the probabilities."
    },
    {
      "start": 133.2,
      "end": 134.9,
      "text": "It does not change what the model learned."
    },
    {
      "start": 136.24,
      "end": 141.38,
      "text": "Now, let's look at the sheer volume of calculations driving these probabilities."
    },
    {
      "start": 142.56,
      "end": 144.98,
      "text": "The training process created the model's weights,"
    },
    {
      "start": 145.54,
      "end": 148.48,
      "text": "the internal numbers that shape every single prediction."
    },
    {
      "start": 149.46,
      "end": 152.0,
      "text": "When you use AI, those weights stay fixed."
    },
    {
      "start": 153.08,
      "end": 155.86,
      "text": "Imagine an example model containing one trillion weights."
    },
    {
      "start": 156.54,
      "end": 158.78,
      "text": "Each time the AI generates a new token,"
    },
    {
      "start": 159.22,
      "end": 162.86,
      "text": "it must run those weights through a massive series of computations."
    },
    {
      "start": 163.42,
      "end": 165.3,
      "text": "Roughly two calculations per weight."
    },
    {
      "start": 165.96,
      "end": 169.56,
      "text": "For a single token, one pass through this trillion weight model"
    },
    {
      "start": 169.56,
      "end": 171.64,
      "text": "equals about two trillion calculations,"
    },
    {
      "start": 172.02,
      "end": 174.32,
      "text": "just to output one word like spot."
    },
    {
      "start": 175.1,
      "end": 177.28,
      "text": "Scale that up to a short AI answer."
    },
    {
      "start": 177.86,
      "end": 184.32,
      "text": "Generating 100 tokens at two trillion calculations each results in roughly 200 trillion calculations."
    },
    {
      "start": 185.06,
      "end": 187.74,
      "text": "For a longer conversation of 1000 tokens,"
    },
    {
      "start": 188.16,
      "end": 191.06,
      "text": "the total reaches approximately two quadrillion calculations."
    },
    {
      "start": 191.72,
      "end": 194.78,
      "text": "These numbers are estimates for an imagined model,"
    },
    {
      "start": 195.2,
      "end": 197.02,
      "text": "not precise measurements of a real one."
    },
    {
      "start": 197.86,
      "end": 202.14,
      "text": "Even with estimates, the sheer density of effort is clear."
    },
    {
      "start": 203.48,
      "end": 207.26,
      "text": "Even a short answer takes trillions of calculations."
    },
    {
      "start": 210.37,
      "end": 211.41,
      "text": "Not a mind."
    },
    {
      "start": 213.75,
      "end": 215.81,
      "text": "At a scale nobody can picture."
    },
    {
      "start": 217.01,
      "end": 219.41,
      "text": "Every time you hit send."
    }
  ],
